WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:02.968
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:04.934
Yeah, you're here.
You made it.

00:00:04.934 --> 00:00:06.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.067 --> 00:00:09.367
♪♪

00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:10.734
It is the holiday season.

00:00:10.734 --> 00:00:12.667
Isn't it a great time
to be here in New York City?

00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:15.033
Doesn't it feel good?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:17.868
But I just saw that the police
just warned tourists

00:00:17.868 --> 00:00:21.100
to be on the lookout
for pickpockets.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:23.200
And to everyone in the audience
who just checked your pockets,

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.234
it's too late now.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.234 --> 00:00:27.734
You can never be too safe.
That's why this time of year,

00:00:27.734 --> 00:00:30.167
instead of a wallet,
I keep all my money in crypto.

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:31.567
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:34.000
That's right.
Pickpockets are everywhere.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.601
'Cause nothing ruins a week
of $200 Broadway tickets

00:00:36.601 --> 00:00:38.701
and $12 pretzels
like getting ripped off.

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:40.267
You know what I'm saying?

00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:42.000
Hey, here's some good news
for the holidays.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.234
After more than a year
of record inflation,

00:00:44.234 --> 00:00:47.334
it looks like prices
are finally starting to go down.

00:00:47.334 --> 00:00:48.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:51.334
Yeah. So...

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:53.000
So, take that, annoying people

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.734
who finished all their
Christmas shopping in November.

00:00:55.734 --> 00:00:59.133
Ha ha!

00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:01.200
We win!

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.567
Some political news.

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:04.234
Tomorrow is
the Georgia Senate runoff

00:01:04.234 --> 00:01:07.501
between Herschel Walker
and Senator Raphael Warnock.

00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:09.300
Warnock's supporters said
that they're voting for him

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:11.801
because of his policies,
while Walker's supporters say

00:01:11.801 --> 00:01:13.767
they're voting for him
because it's funny.

00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:15.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.734 --> 00:01:19.000
More than 1.8 million Georgia
residents have already voted,

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:21.133
and that's just
Herschel Walker's children.

00:01:21.133 --> 00:01:23.000
[ Audience oohs ]
Right now --

00:01:23.067 --> 00:01:25.567
[ Applause ]
Right now --

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:27.067
-Whoa!

00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:29.200
-Right now,
Warnock is leading Walker

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.300
in the polls by about 4 points.

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:33.133
Yeah, only 4 points.

00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:34.901
That explains
Warnock's slogan...

00:01:37.534 --> 00:01:39.501
It's like -- It's only 4 points.

00:01:39.501 --> 00:01:40.901
Tomorrow is the big runoff

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:42.601
between Herschel Walker
and Raphael Warnock.

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:44.767
And I must say,
it's nice to see two candidates

00:01:44.767 --> 00:01:46.200
set aside their personal attacks

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:48.200
and focus on real issues
in their campaign.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:50.200
Check out this ad
for Herschel Walker.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:52.901
-Herschel Walker
has always let Georgians know

00:01:52.901 --> 00:01:55.133
where he stands
on the important issues

00:01:55.133 --> 00:01:56.834
like taxes, jobs...

00:01:56.834 --> 00:01:58.100
and vampires.
-[ Hissing ]

00:01:58.100 --> 00:01:59.300
-I don't know if you know.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:00.934
Vampires are some cool people,
are they not?

00:02:00.934 --> 00:02:02.901
But I'm-a tell you something
today I found out.

00:02:02.901 --> 00:02:05.467
A werewolf can kill a vampire.
Do you know that?

00:02:05.467 --> 00:02:08.033
-Where does Raphael Warnock
stand on vampires?

00:02:08.033 --> 00:02:10.400
He's never told us.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.434
But Herschel Walker has.

00:02:12.434 --> 00:02:13.834
-Because, you know,
gotta have a stake

00:02:13.834 --> 00:02:16.067
and gotta have a thing
that kill 'em in the heart.

00:02:16.067 --> 00:02:18.467
And you got a necklace of
garlic, 'cause that work.

00:02:18.467 --> 00:02:20.033
I don't know what it does,
but it work.

00:02:20.033 --> 00:02:22.334
Gotta have a cross 'cause
it burns. I know that works.

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:28.534
-So I don't want to be
a vampire anymore.

00:02:28.534 --> 00:02:29.667
I want to be a werewolf.

00:02:29.667 --> 00:02:31.767
[ Wolf howls ]

00:02:31.767 --> 00:02:33.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:37.701 --> 00:02:39.200
-Well, everyone's
talking about this.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.801
Over the weekend,
former President Trump

00:02:40.801 --> 00:02:43.400
called for the 2020 election
to be overturned

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.367
by terminating the Constitution.

00:02:45.367 --> 00:02:46.801
[ Audience oohs ]

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:48.868
And Trump can actually do it
because he has the real

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:51.100
Constitution hanging in
the bathroom at Mar-a-Lago.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:52.968
[ Laughter ]
So he could...

00:02:54.634 --> 00:02:57.033
Trump wants to terminate
the Constitution.

00:02:57.033 --> 00:02:58.801
Then a staffer held a brick
to his ear like,

00:02:58.801 --> 00:03:01.234
"Yeah, working on it
right now, sir. Yeah."

00:03:01.234 --> 00:03:02.767
Well, listen to this.
I read that compared

00:03:02.767 --> 00:03:04.834
to past presidents,
books about President Biden

00:03:04.834 --> 00:03:07.267
aren't selling many copies.

00:03:07.267 --> 00:03:09.834
Yeah, you can tell that Biden
books aren't that exciting.

00:03:09.834 --> 00:03:11.300
I mean, just look
at the blurbs on the back.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.501
For instance, this critic from
"The New York Times" wrote...

00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:17.901
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:17.901 --> 00:03:19.534
Next up,
"The Washington Post" wrote...

00:03:22.834 --> 00:03:24.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:24.834 --> 00:03:26.701
Then "USA Today" wrote...

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:31.934
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Wow!

00:03:31.934 --> 00:03:33.267
-These are the blurbs
on the back of --

00:03:33.267 --> 00:03:34.801
-These are the blurbs
on the back of the book

00:03:34.801 --> 00:03:36.467
that real humans wrote. Wow.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:37.934
"Time" Magazine wrote...

00:03:41.701 --> 00:03:42.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:42.968 --> 00:03:45.200
And finally,
the "Chicago Tribune" wrote...

00:03:48.267 --> 00:03:49.934
I mean, why would you put that
on the back of the --

00:03:49.934 --> 00:03:50.968
-Wow.

00:03:50.968 --> 00:03:52.434
[ Applause ]

00:03:52.434 --> 00:03:53.801
-Some entertainment news.

00:03:53.801 --> 00:03:56.100
A new episode of "White Lotus"
dropped last night,

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.667
and it was a real doozy.

00:03:57.667 --> 00:03:59.701
-Oh, no. No spoilers.
I haven't seen it yet.

00:03:59.701 --> 00:04:01.467
-Oh, I wasn't
gonna spoil anything.

00:04:01.467 --> 00:04:02.801
I was just saying
it was a good episode. I --

00:04:02.801 --> 00:04:04.400
-I don't care.
I might be able

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:07.734
to extrapolate information
from what you say.

00:04:07.734 --> 00:04:09.167
-I don't see
how that's possible.

00:04:09.167 --> 00:04:11.367
-Just don't. Okay?

00:04:11.367 --> 00:04:12.968
-Alright. Fine.
What else can we talk about?

00:04:12.968 --> 00:04:14.701
Everyone's talking
about the show "Wednesday" --

00:04:14.701 --> 00:04:17.734
-Ah, wah-wah-wah! No spoilers.

00:04:17.734 --> 00:04:20.400
-I was just gonna say the dance
scene is getting a lot of buzz.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:23.901
-Great, Jimmy. Now I know
there's a dance scene.

00:04:23.901 --> 00:04:25.400
-Everyone knows
there's a dance scene.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:27.634
It's huge on TikTok.
-Great!

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:30.701
Now I know it was huge
on TikTok!

00:04:30.701 --> 00:04:32.434
-Alright. Fine. What else
is there to talk about?

00:04:32.434 --> 00:04:35.968
"Yellowstone" is big right now.
-Ahh-- I haven't seen it.

00:04:35.968 --> 00:04:37.400
-"Violent Night"
is getting good reviews.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:40.067
-Haven't seen it.

00:04:40.067 --> 00:04:41.534
-The trailer for "Cocaine Bear."

00:04:41.534 --> 00:04:43.601
-♪ La dee da dee da da da ♪

00:04:43.601 --> 00:04:45.167
-The "Survivor" finale is --

00:04:45.167 --> 00:04:46.834
-♪ Loo loo loo loo,
loo loo loo loo loo ♪

00:04:46.834 --> 00:04:48.434
-Alright. Fine. Fine. We'll talk
about the news instead.

00:04:48.434 --> 00:04:51.801
Alright? Everyone knows the U.S.
lost to the Netherlands.

00:04:51.801 --> 00:04:53.100
-In what?

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:54.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.834 --> 00:04:57.601
[ Applause ]

00:04:57.601 --> 00:04:59.000
-President Joe Biden --

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.868
-He won the election?

00:05:00.868 --> 00:05:02.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.167 --> 00:05:03.567
-Donald Trump --

00:05:03.567 --> 00:05:05.868
-He won the election?!

00:05:05.868 --> 00:05:08.400
-Christmas is almost here.
-It is?

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:10.300
-Alright. That's enough.
You're behind on everything.

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:11.834
What have you been doing
this whole time?

00:05:11.834 --> 00:05:16.534
-Wordle. I'm actually doing
today's puzzle right now.

00:05:16.534 --> 00:05:18.501
-Well, get a load of this.
It's actually woken.

00:05:18.501 --> 00:05:21.634
W-O-K-E-N.
"Woken" is the word today.

00:05:21.634 --> 00:05:23.834
-I swear to God.

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:26.934
Mother [bleep]!

00:05:26.934 --> 00:05:30.767
-Hey, hey, hey! Hey, hey!
Come on, man! Whoa! Hey!

00:05:30.767 --> 00:05:33.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:35.234
Sorry!

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:37.801
Unbelievable. Sorry!

00:05:39.434 --> 00:05:41.534
-Steve: Wow.
-Guys, get this.

00:05:41.534 --> 00:05:44.067
Following a pause
during the pandemic,

00:05:44.067 --> 00:05:46.167
the Catholic Church
has reintroduced handshakes

00:05:46.167 --> 00:05:47.467
during mass.

00:05:47.467 --> 00:05:49.901
-[ Applause ]
-[ Woman exclaims ]

00:05:49.901 --> 00:05:52.033
-Really?
-Wow.

00:05:52.033 --> 00:05:54.033
-Peace be with you. Wow.

00:05:54.033 --> 00:05:55.434
-Yep, shaking hands at church,

00:05:55.434 --> 00:05:57.701
or as Mike Pence calls it,
"going all the way."

00:05:57.701 --> 00:05:59.801
[ Laughter ]
Hey. Did you guys see this?

00:05:59.801 --> 00:06:02.000
Everyone's been using
this new A.I. app

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.400
that takes your selfies

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:05.167
and turns them
into beautiful portraits.

00:06:05.167 --> 00:06:07.334
I did mine earlier today.
Look at -- Look at mine.

00:06:07.334 --> 00:06:10.934
They made me look like a...
1930s Hollywood star.

00:06:10.934 --> 00:06:12.133
-Oh.
-Quest, did you try it?

00:06:12.133 --> 00:06:14.200
-Yeah, I did.
Check it out, man.

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:15.567
-Ooh.
-See?

00:06:15.567 --> 00:06:17.501
That's what I look like
as an impressionist painting.

00:06:17.501 --> 00:06:19.300
-Yeah, I love that.
Higgins, did you try it?

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:21.868
-Yeah. Take a look.

00:06:21.868 --> 00:06:23.501
-Hey! God!

00:06:25.968 --> 00:06:28.234
What filter is that?!

00:06:28.234 --> 00:06:30.367
-Filter?
That was Saturday.

00:06:30.367 --> 00:06:32.000
-Oh, my God!

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:33.534
Moving on.
[ Clears throat ]

00:06:37.067 --> 00:06:39.901
Hey, guys, I heard about a
tattoo removal studio in London

00:06:39.901 --> 00:06:42.868
that's lasering off
Kanye West tattoos for free.

00:06:42.868 --> 00:06:45.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:45.467 --> 00:06:49.033
That's great. You just walk in
and say, "Make my Ye a nay."

00:06:49.033 --> 00:06:51.067
♪♪

00:06:51.067 --> 00:06:52.400
For the first time
in three years,

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:54.767
office holiday parties are back.

00:06:54.767 --> 00:06:58.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:58.701 --> 00:07:00.501
Yep, it's that magical night
when you say,

00:07:00.501 --> 00:07:02.667
"let's not talk about work"
and then only talk about work.

00:07:02.667 --> 00:07:04.300
[ Laughter ]

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:06.200
Yeah, it's the same
conversations you have at work,

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:07.434
but now they're an inch
from your ear

00:07:07.434 --> 00:07:08.767
and 10 times the volume.

00:07:08.767 --> 00:07:10.667
-[ Loud music plays ]
-"I'm thinking about following

00:07:10.667 --> 00:07:12.434
up with Brian about that raise!"

00:07:12.434 --> 00:07:14.400
[ Laughter ]

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:15.567
[ Music stops ]

00:07:15.567 --> 00:07:18.167
[ Laughter ]

00:07:18.167 --> 00:07:20.934
That's right. The party is
basically this meme,

00:07:20.934 --> 00:07:22.367
plus Santa hats.

00:07:22.367 --> 00:07:24.534
[ Laughter ]

00:07:24.534 --> 00:07:26.968
Yep, every office holiday party
is the same.

00:07:26.968 --> 00:07:28.567
They all start
with a champagne toast

00:07:28.567 --> 00:07:31.467
and end with half the staff
updating their LinkedIn.

00:07:31.467 --> 00:07:33.934
The White House chief of staff
said that he expects

00:07:33.934 --> 00:07:36.834
President Biden to announce that
he's running for re-election

00:07:36.834 --> 00:07:38.400
after the holidays.

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:39.801
That makes sense.

00:07:39.801 --> 00:07:41.367
Most Americans announce that
they're gonna start running

00:07:41.367 --> 00:07:42.667
after the holidays.

00:07:42.667 --> 00:07:45.367
[ Laughter ]

00:07:45.367 --> 00:07:47.467
Also, I'm no political expert,
but if you announce that

00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:48.868
you're going to make
an announcement,

00:07:48.868 --> 00:07:50.334
isn't that the announcement?

00:07:50.334 --> 00:07:51.767
[ Laughter ]

00:07:51.767 --> 00:07:53.968
Speaking of running for
president, new polling shows

00:07:53.968 --> 00:07:57.000
that in a potential 2024
matchup, Biden is tied with

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:58.767
Florida governor Ron DeSantis,

00:07:58.767 --> 00:08:02.367
while DeSantis leads former
president Trump by 10 points.

00:08:02.367 --> 00:08:04.467
-Ooh.
-Yep, Biden, DeSantis,

00:08:04.467 --> 00:08:06.934
and Trump -- it's like your
grandfather, your crazy uncle,

00:08:06.934 --> 00:08:08.868
and the family member
nobody talks about anymore.

00:08:08.868 --> 00:08:11.767
[ Laughter ]

00:08:11.767 --> 00:08:16.100
Yep, Trump's unfavorable rating
has surged to 67%.

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:19.334
To give you an idea of how bad
that is, Kanye is only at 66.

00:08:19.334 --> 00:08:20.334
[ Laughter ]

00:08:20.334 --> 00:08:22.667
Bad.

00:08:22.667 --> 00:08:26.067
Some more 2024 news -- former
Trump national security adviser

00:08:26.067 --> 00:08:27.367
John Bolton said that

00:08:27.367 --> 00:08:29.000
he's considering running
for president.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:31.467
He's even been testing out
some campaign slogans

00:08:31.467 --> 00:08:32.868
to see what people respond to.

00:08:32.868 --> 00:08:34.067
Check these out.
First there's...

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:42.300
[ Laughter ]

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:43.601
Then there's...

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:49.467
-Oh!
-[ Laughter ]

00:08:49.467 --> 00:08:50.801
-And finally, there's...

00:08:54.467 --> 00:08:56.434
[ Laughter ]

00:08:56.434 --> 00:08:59.067
"Anything!
You'll never get it from me!"

00:08:59.067 --> 00:09:01.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:01.901 --> 00:09:04.133
That's right, John Bolton said
that he's considering

00:09:04.133 --> 00:09:06.567
a 2024 presidential run
to challenge Trump.

00:09:06.567 --> 00:09:07.767
Can we see Bolton?

00:09:07.767 --> 00:09:09.434
There he is.
Yeah, well, he --

00:09:09.434 --> 00:09:10.767
He already has
a fair amount of support.

00:09:10.767 --> 00:09:12.701
Check out what some of
his supporters are saying.

00:09:12.701 --> 00:09:14.100
First up, Geraldo Rivera said...

00:09:18.601 --> 00:09:20.000
Then actor Sam Elliott said...

00:09:21.434 --> 00:09:24.200
[ Laughter ]

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:25.868
And singer David Crosby said...

00:09:29.701 --> 00:09:31.000
Then Hulk Hogan said...

00:09:32.467 --> 00:09:35.033
[ Laughter ]

00:09:35.033 --> 00:09:36.400
Then the Monopoly Man said...

00:09:38.968 --> 00:09:45.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:47.267
And finally, the Lorax said...

00:09:48.534 --> 00:09:49.767
[ Laughter ]

00:09:49.767 --> 00:09:51.200
Can't help it.

00:09:52.901 --> 00:09:54.367
Did you guys see this?
This is real.

00:09:54.367 --> 00:09:57.834
During a hearing, Rudy Giuliani
was caught on a hot mike telling

00:09:57.834 --> 00:10:00.667
his lawyer that he accidentally
wore two watches.

00:10:00.667 --> 00:10:01.801
[ Laughter ]

00:10:01.801 --> 00:10:03.601
Now, the quality of the footage
is bad,

00:10:03.601 --> 00:10:05.400
but it doesn't disappoint.
Check this out.

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:08.000
-So, I'm at a good place
to stop, Mr. Chair.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:09.567
-Thank you.

00:10:13.534 --> 00:10:15.267
You know I have two watches on?

00:10:15.267 --> 00:10:19.801
[ Laughter ]

00:10:19.801 --> 00:10:21.100
-What?

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:23.601
-Just a reminder, that was
Trump's top lawyer.

00:10:23.601 --> 00:10:25.133
[ Laughter ]

00:10:25.133 --> 00:10:27.300
Two watches.
-Ah.

00:10:27.300 --> 00:10:28.801
-Oh, this is very cool.

00:10:28.801 --> 00:10:31.234
Researchers in Germany have
developed Golfi,

00:10:31.234 --> 00:10:33.968
a golfing robot that can make
perfect putts.

00:10:33.968 --> 00:10:35.634
-Hmm.
-Yeah. And that's not all.

00:10:35.634 --> 00:10:37.334
Here's a full list of
what Golfi can do.

00:10:37.334 --> 00:10:39.400
It can, of course, play golf,

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:42.834
or it can put his hand
on your shoulder.

00:10:42.834 --> 00:10:45.734
It can say,
"I'm proud of you, son."

00:10:45.734 --> 00:10:47.367
[ Laughter ]

00:10:47.367 --> 00:10:49.934
And it can kiss your mom.

00:10:49.934 --> 00:10:51.968
Wait, kiss your mom?

00:10:51.968 --> 00:10:54.567
Yup. Now Golfi's moving in.

00:10:54.567 --> 00:10:55.934
He's calling you "champ"

00:10:55.934 --> 00:10:57.734
and showing up to
your baseball games.

00:10:57.734 --> 00:10:59.200
"Great catch, kid,
but you really

00:10:59.200 --> 00:11:00.634
should have thrown to third."

00:11:00.634 --> 00:11:02.300
"Shut up!
You're not my real dad!"

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:04.667
"Yes, I am. Why do you think
you have robot legs?"

00:11:04.667 --> 00:11:07.167
Look down.
Oh, God, you do have robot legs.

00:11:07.167 --> 00:11:08.968
Robot arms, robot face.

00:11:08.968 --> 00:11:10.501
He's right. You're not human.

00:11:10.501 --> 00:11:12.033
You're Golfi Jr.

00:11:12.033 --> 00:11:19.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:19.934 --> 00:11:21.367
Well, here's some good news.

00:11:21.367 --> 00:11:24.501
I saw that the head of the CDC
said the updated flu vaccine

00:11:24.501 --> 00:11:27.801
looks like a very good match
for this year's strains.

00:11:27.801 --> 00:11:29.767
Basically the vaccine saw
the strains

00:11:29.767 --> 00:11:30.968
and was like, "Swipe right."

00:11:30.968 --> 00:11:32.534
[ Laughter ]

00:11:32.534 --> 00:11:34.901
It's not a perfect match,
but like most people, the flu is

00:11:34.901 --> 00:11:36.934
just happy to go home with
someone for the holidays.

00:11:36.934 --> 00:11:38.734
[ Laughter ]

00:11:38.734 --> 00:11:39.901
Well, guys, get this.

00:11:39.901 --> 00:11:42.334
"Dahmer" just became
the third show on Netflix

00:11:42.334 --> 00:11:45.601
to hit 1 billion hours
viewed in 60 days.

00:11:45.601 --> 00:11:47.501
-Wow!
-And if someone mentions that

00:11:47.501 --> 00:11:49.968
at the office holiday party,
do not split an Uber home.

00:11:49.968 --> 00:11:51.133
[ Laughter ]

00:11:51.133 --> 00:11:52.501
♪♪

00:11:52.501 --> 00:11:55.400
Guys, we're right in the middle
of the holiday season.

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:57.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
Do you feel the vibes?

00:11:57.534 --> 00:12:00.200
And if you're waiting to buy
a Christmas tree,

00:12:00.200 --> 00:12:03.067
you better hurry, because due to
high demand and low supply,

00:12:03.067 --> 00:12:04.968
prices are soaring.

00:12:04.968 --> 00:12:06.567
Yeah.
I'm trying to get ahead of this.

00:12:06.567 --> 00:12:08.000
That's why every night,
on the way home,

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:09.133
I cut one branch off

00:12:09.133 --> 00:12:10.834
the Rockefeller Center
Christmas Tree.

00:12:10.834 --> 00:12:12.834
I just take it away from there.

00:12:13.934 --> 00:12:15.734
I'm getting there.

00:12:15.734 --> 00:12:18.000
♪ Christmastime ♪

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:19.133
[ Laughter ]

00:12:19.133 --> 00:12:20.534
Yeah, it's the holiday season,

00:12:20.534 --> 00:12:22.667
and today, New York
got an early Christmas gift.

00:12:22.667 --> 00:12:25.267
Aaron Judge is coming back
to the Yankees!

00:12:25.267 --> 00:12:27.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:28.667
Yes!

00:12:31.167 --> 00:12:32.601
That's right.

00:12:32.601 --> 00:12:35.834
Yankees superstar Aaron Judge
has decided to stay in New York,

00:12:35.834 --> 00:12:40.033
agreeing to a nine-year,
$360 million contract.

00:12:40.033 --> 00:12:42.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:42.601 --> 00:12:44.000
When he heard that,
Babe Ruth said, "What the hell?

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:45.968
I got paid in peanuts and
Cracker Jacks."

00:12:45.968 --> 00:12:48.167
[ Laughter ]

00:12:48.167 --> 00:12:49.934
$360 million.

00:12:49.934 --> 00:12:51.934
Today, Judge walked into
the owner's office and said,

00:12:51.934 --> 00:12:54.000
"You're in my seat."
[ Laughter ]

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:55.100
What a deal.

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:56.467
Aaron is now the only person

00:12:56.467 --> 00:12:58.100
who can afford a beer
in Yankee Stadium.

00:12:58.100 --> 00:13:00.300
-Oh!
-Yeah.

00:13:00.300 --> 00:13:01.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:13:01.367 --> 00:13:02.968
It's true.

00:13:05.868 --> 00:13:08.267
The good news is,
Judge got $360 million.

00:13:08.267 --> 00:13:09.868
The bad news is,
the rest of the team

00:13:09.868 --> 00:13:11.501
is now getting paid in crypto.

00:13:11.501 --> 00:13:13.601
[ Laughter ]

00:13:13.601 --> 00:13:15.601
Did you guys hear about this?

00:13:15.601 --> 00:13:17.567
Apparently, former president
Trump's lawyers

00:13:17.567 --> 00:13:20.601
just turned over more
classified items to the FBI

00:13:20.601 --> 00:13:23.534
after finding them at
Trump's storage unit in Florida.

00:13:23.534 --> 00:13:24.834
[ Laughter ]

00:13:24.834 --> 00:13:26.300
Yeah, we were just
a week away from

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:27.968
our most classified secrets
ending up on

00:13:27.968 --> 00:13:30.100
an episode of "Storage Wars."

00:13:30.100 --> 00:13:32.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:13:32.767 --> 00:13:36.501
I mean, really.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:13:36.501 --> 00:13:39.033
A storage unit.
A storage unit.

00:13:39.033 --> 00:13:41.200
You know that you've stolen
too many top secret documents

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:42.701
when you can't even fit them
all in your house.

00:13:42.701 --> 00:13:44.667
You know what I'm saying?

00:13:44.667 --> 00:13:47.467
Meanwhile, last night, Trump
hosted an event at Mar-a-Lago

00:13:47.467 --> 00:13:51.000
that featured a prominent
QAnon conspiracy theorist.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:53.567
It's not good when you mingle
with a conspiracy theorist

00:13:53.567 --> 00:13:55.801
to distract from your dinner
with a white supremacist.

00:13:55.801 --> 00:13:57.200
You know what I'm saying?

00:13:57.200 --> 00:13:59.467
Hey, guys, get this --
airline passengers in Europe

00:13:59.467 --> 00:14:01.734
will soon be allowed
to use 5G service

00:14:01.734 --> 00:14:03.801
to make phone calls on board.

00:14:03.801 --> 00:14:06.801
The only thing worse than your
seatmate trying to talk to you

00:14:06.801 --> 00:14:08.634
is your seatmate
trying to talk to someone else.

00:14:08.634 --> 00:14:10.000
It's like,
"Hey, can you hear me?!

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:12.367
I'm on a plane right now!"

00:14:13.701 --> 00:14:16.834
Yeah, this means no more putting
your phone on airplane mode.

00:14:16.834 --> 00:14:18.100
Yep, everyone's like, "Finally,

00:14:18.100 --> 00:14:19.467
we can stop pretending
to do that."

00:14:19.467 --> 00:14:21.634
[ Laughter ]

00:14:21.634 --> 00:14:23.033
Good.

00:14:23.033 --> 00:14:24.234
Some entertainment news.

00:14:24.234 --> 00:14:26.267
"Wednesday" is on track
to become Netflix's

00:14:26.267 --> 00:14:29.701
most-watched English-language
TV series ever.

00:14:29.701 --> 00:14:31.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:14:34.968 --> 00:14:36.634
You know these
are crazy times when a show

00:14:36.634 --> 00:14:39.400
about a depressed goth child is
what makes us all happy.

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:41.234
[ Laughter ]

00:14:41.234 --> 00:14:42.534
I mean...

00:14:42.534 --> 00:14:44.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:14:44.667 --> 00:14:46.501
It's good, it's good.

00:14:46.501 --> 00:14:48.901
Everyone's talking about
the holiday action movie

00:14:48.901 --> 00:14:50.567
"Violent Night," as well.

00:14:50.567 --> 00:14:52.467
It did surprisingly well
at the box office,

00:14:52.467 --> 00:14:55.033
so they're re-editing
old holiday favorites now

00:14:55.033 --> 00:14:56.901
to capitalize on this new trend.

00:14:56.901 --> 00:14:58.801
-Really?
-Look at this ad I saw today.

00:14:58.801 --> 00:15:01.467
-They tried to take
everything he had,

00:15:01.467 --> 00:15:05.167
but this Christmas,
George Bailey fights back.

00:15:05.167 --> 00:15:08.000
He's smooth-talking,
hard-drinking,

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:10.334
and he's got a message
for anyone who crosses him.

00:15:10.334 --> 00:15:12.267
-You're going to die!
-[ Screams ]

00:15:14.934 --> 00:15:18.501
-Every time a bell rings,
George kicks some ass.

00:15:19.701 --> 00:15:22.300
-Where's that money,
you stupid old [bleep]

00:15:22.300 --> 00:15:24.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:15:24.667 --> 00:15:27.000
-Wow.
-Wow!

00:15:29.934 --> 00:15:31.901
"Stupid old --" beep!

00:15:31.901 --> 00:15:33.701
-"Where's that money at?"

00:15:33.701 --> 00:15:36.200
Right now, a lot of people are
putting out holiday decorations.

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:37.934
I saw one homeowner
in Wisconsin --

00:15:37.934 --> 00:15:39.234
this made me laugh --
who kept it very simple.

00:15:39.234 --> 00:15:40.267
Look at this video.

00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:49.901
[ Laughter ]

00:15:49.901 --> 00:15:50.901
♪♪

00:15:50.901 --> 00:15:53.267
That's fantastic.

00:15:53.267 --> 00:15:56.000
That's the most effort someone's
ever put into no effort.

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:57.133
♪♪

00:15:57.133 --> 00:15:58.501
Well, I'm in
a good mood right now

00:15:58.501 --> 00:15:59.968
because we're right in
the middle of

00:15:59.968 --> 00:16:02.100
the holiday season right now,
and I love the holiday season.

00:16:02.100 --> 00:16:05.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
I love it.

00:16:05.467 --> 00:16:07.934
By the way, here's a little tip
for anyone buying presents.

00:16:07.934 --> 00:16:09.868
Whatever you buy,
just say you got it on Etsy

00:16:09.868 --> 00:16:12.200
so everyone thinks a lot of
thought went into it.

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:13.501
That's what I do.

00:16:13.501 --> 00:16:17.033
Of course, gift cards
are always a popular option.

00:16:17.033 --> 00:16:18.667
And I like
the Amazon gift cards,

00:16:18.667 --> 00:16:20.367
because they basically say,
"The only thing

00:16:20.367 --> 00:16:22.734
I 100% know about you
is that you want a gift."

00:16:22.734 --> 00:16:24.234
[ Laughter ]

00:16:24.234 --> 00:16:27.234
Meanwhile, I saw that tomorrow
is National Christmas Card Day.

00:16:27.234 --> 00:16:28.300
And I've already seen some

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:29.767
pretty interesting cards
this year.

00:16:29.767 --> 00:16:31.267
I'll show you some of the
ones I've got.

00:16:31.267 --> 00:16:33.667
For instance, look at this.
This is a card from Aaron Judge.

00:16:33.667 --> 00:16:34.767
On the front, it says...

00:16:37.167 --> 00:16:38.267
Open it up, and it says...

00:16:41.767 --> 00:16:43.400
You go, "Wait. Come on."

00:16:43.400 --> 00:16:45.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:16:45.067 --> 00:16:47.334
Here's another one I got.
-They're very specific, yeah.

00:16:47.334 --> 00:16:48.567
-Here's a card from
"Good Morning America."

00:16:48.567 --> 00:16:49.601
It says...

00:16:51.601 --> 00:16:53.167
You open it up, it says...

00:16:55.067 --> 00:16:56.834
[ Laughter ]

00:16:56.834 --> 00:16:57.868
-Wow!

00:16:57.868 --> 00:16:59.701
-I don't know what it means.

00:16:59.701 --> 00:17:02.334
-Morning.
-Here's a card from Joe Biden.

00:17:02.334 --> 00:17:03.334
It says...

00:17:05.367 --> 00:17:06.467
You open it up, it says...

00:17:14.767 --> 00:17:16.801
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:17:16.801 --> 00:17:18.467
Wow.

00:17:22.067 --> 00:17:23.868
Here's a nice card
I got from Elon Musk.

00:17:23.868 --> 00:17:24.934
It says...

00:17:26.300 --> 00:17:27.400
Open it up, it says...

00:17:28.534 --> 00:17:30.434
-Wow!
-That's nice.

00:17:33.133 --> 00:17:35.000
Here's a card from
Herschel Walker. It says...

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:38.334
Open it up, it says...

00:17:39.334 --> 00:17:40.400
And you know what?

00:17:40.400 --> 00:17:43.167
He's trying.
[ Laughter ]

00:17:43.167 --> 00:17:44.634
He's trying.
-He's trying.

00:17:44.634 --> 00:17:46.234
He falls down, he gets back up.
-Yeah.

00:17:46.234 --> 00:17:47.634
And, finally, here's a card
from Vice President Harris.

00:17:47.634 --> 00:17:48.634
It says...

00:17:50.534 --> 00:17:51.667
Open it up, it says...

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:56.334
Everyone's in the spirit.
Very nice.

00:17:56.334 --> 00:17:57.634
♪♪

00:17:57.634 --> 00:17:59.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:17:59.234 --> 00:18:01.667
Let's get to some news.
Everybody's talking about this.

00:18:01.667 --> 00:18:04.567
Today, 10 months after
she was detained,

00:18:04.567 --> 00:18:08.067
Brittney Griner
was freed from Russian custody

00:18:08.067 --> 00:18:09.501
in a prisoner exchange...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:18:09.501 --> 00:18:11.033
♪♪

00:18:11.033 --> 00:18:12.701
...between The White House
and the Kremlin.

00:18:12.701 --> 00:18:14.133
You could tell Biden
was fired up

00:18:14.133 --> 00:18:17.167
when he began his speech with,
"It's Brittney [bleep]"

00:18:17.167 --> 00:18:18.501
And you go, "Hey."

00:18:18.501 --> 00:18:20.400
[ Laughter ]

00:18:20.400 --> 00:18:22.400
Putin is no stranger
to prisoner swaps.

00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:23.767
In fact, "Prisoner Swap"

00:18:23.767 --> 00:18:26.334
is the most popular
reality show in Russia.

00:18:26.334 --> 00:18:28.767
Yeah, there was a prisoner swap.

00:18:28.767 --> 00:18:31.033
In exchange for Griner,
Moscow received

00:18:31.033 --> 00:18:33.133
the notorious Russian
arms dealer

00:18:33.133 --> 00:18:35.067
who is known as
"The Merchant of Death."

00:18:35.067 --> 00:18:37.334
-Ooh!
-Can we see what he looks like?

00:18:37.334 --> 00:18:38.634
-Ooh!

00:18:38.634 --> 00:18:40.467
[ Laughter ]

00:18:40.467 --> 00:18:41.767
-When asked for a statement,
he said,

00:18:41.767 --> 00:18:44.033
"If your wife has ever said,
'Come move these

00:18:44.033 --> 00:18:46.467
rocket launchers
so I can take a bath,'

00:18:46.467 --> 00:18:48.767
you might be
an international arms dealer."

00:18:48.767 --> 00:18:53.133
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:18:53.133 --> 00:18:55.667
Hey, I read that the C.E.O.
of Build-A-Bear Workshop

00:18:55.667 --> 00:18:59.868
said 40% of their shoppers are
now teenagers and adults.

00:18:59.868 --> 00:19:01.067
It's little surprising,

00:19:01.067 --> 00:19:02.467
but it does explain
the new ad campaign.

00:19:02.467 --> 00:19:03.701
Check this out.

00:19:03.701 --> 00:19:06.868
-At Build-A-Bear Workshop,
we're not just for kids.

00:19:06.868 --> 00:19:08.601
We're for kids of all ages,

00:19:08.601 --> 00:19:10.267
so the next time
you're at the mall,

00:19:10.267 --> 00:19:12.434
stop on by and build a bear.

00:19:12.434 --> 00:19:13.567
Build a bestie.

00:19:13.567 --> 00:19:14.634
Build a boss.

00:19:14.634 --> 00:19:15.968
Build a boyfriend.

00:19:15.968 --> 00:19:18.501
Build a better life,
the one you used to dream about

00:19:18.501 --> 00:19:20.868
back when everything
still felt exciting and vital,

00:19:20.868 --> 00:19:23.200
because age is nothing
but a number,

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:25.300
a big, terrible number,

00:19:25.300 --> 00:19:27.634
a grandfather clock
about to strike,

00:19:27.634 --> 00:19:31.067
the sound of whose
bong, bong, bong

00:19:31.067 --> 00:19:33.601
will never be heard by
the lifeless bear

00:19:33.601 --> 00:19:36.367
you clutch to as a totem of
what was once possible

00:19:36.367 --> 00:19:37.901
but no longer is.

00:19:37.901 --> 00:19:39.267
Build-A-Bear Workshop --

00:19:39.267 --> 00:19:41.133
we're going
through something right now.

00:19:41.133 --> 00:19:43.934
-Wow!
-That explains it.

00:19:43.934 --> 00:19:46.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Wow!

00:19:47.334 --> 00:19:49.133
-Well, guys,
"Avatar: The Way of Water"

00:19:49.133 --> 00:19:50.534
finally comes out next week.

00:19:50.534 --> 00:19:51.767
A lot of people are
excited for it.

00:19:51.767 --> 00:19:52.968
It's getting great reviews.

00:19:52.968 --> 00:19:55.334
But since it's been
almost exactly 13 years

00:19:55.334 --> 00:19:57.501
since "Avatar" came out,
we thought it'd be helpful

00:19:57.501 --> 00:19:59.434
to recap what happened
in the first movie.

00:19:59.434 --> 00:20:02.567
So here now with a rap recap
is Tariq from The Roots.

00:20:02.567 --> 00:20:04.701
Take it away, Tariq.
-One, two, three.

00:20:04.701 --> 00:20:07.334
-♪ I said, I don't remember ♪

00:20:07.334 --> 00:20:09.367
[ Music stops ]

00:20:09.367 --> 00:20:11.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:20:15.734 --> 00:20:17.734
[ Laughter ]

00:20:20.667 --> 00:20:23.567
-I heard about a man in Florida
who was arrested for

00:20:23.567 --> 00:20:24.834
allegedly stealing over

00:20:24.834 --> 00:20:28.634
$1,300 worth of
toothbrushes from Walgreens.

00:20:28.634 --> 00:20:30.133
Yep, the man was convicted after

00:20:30.133 --> 00:20:32.133
four out of five jurors
found him guilty.

00:20:32.133 --> 00:20:33.133
♪♪

00:20:33.133 --> 00:20:34.234
Guys, it's that time of year.

00:20:34.234 --> 00:20:35.934
Tomorrow is SantaCon...

00:20:35.934 --> 00:20:37.367
[ Audience laughs, groans ]

00:20:37.367 --> 00:20:39.367
...here in New York City.

00:20:39.367 --> 00:20:40.467
[ Laughter ]

00:20:40.467 --> 00:20:41.968
You already know what it is.

00:20:41.968 --> 00:20:44.901
Yeah, at SantaCon, thousands of
people will dress up as Santa

00:20:44.901 --> 00:20:48.334
and pack the streets
for an all-day bar crawl.

00:20:48.334 --> 00:20:50.000
So, before you go to bed,
make sure you put out

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:52.667
a plate of Advil
and a tall glass of Pedialyte.

00:20:52.667 --> 00:20:54.234
[ Laughter ]

00:20:54.234 --> 00:20:55.567
That's right, happy SantaCon.

00:20:55.567 --> 00:20:57.501
To everyone in their 20s,
have fun.

00:20:57.501 --> 00:21:00.434
To everyone in their 30s,
it's getting kind of sad.

00:21:00.434 --> 00:21:02.033
[ Laughter ]

00:21:02.033 --> 00:21:03.534
Hey, get this,
according to a new survey,

00:21:03.534 --> 00:21:05.834
30% of Americans
have injured themselves

00:21:05.834 --> 00:21:08.734
during holiday-related
activities.

00:21:08.734 --> 00:21:11.801
While the other 70% are the ones
filming it for TikTok.

00:21:11.801 --> 00:21:13.000
[ Laughter ]

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:15.634
That's right, 30% get injured.

00:21:15.634 --> 00:21:17.300
Who knew climbing a ladder
and hanging lights

00:21:17.300 --> 00:21:19.334
on an icy gutter
could be dangerous?

00:21:19.334 --> 00:21:20.334
[ Laughter ]

00:21:20.334 --> 00:21:21.667
Actually, the most common injury

00:21:21.667 --> 00:21:23.667
is spraining your face
from fake smiling

00:21:23.667 --> 00:21:25.133
after opening a present.

00:21:25.133 --> 00:21:28.200
[ Laughter ]

00:21:28.200 --> 00:21:29.801
"It's a Slanket.
Oh, cool.

00:21:29.801 --> 00:21:32.834
I -- I'll google it,
and I love it."

00:21:32.834 --> 00:21:34.501
Speaking of the holidays,
this weekend

00:21:34.501 --> 00:21:36.300
First Lady Jill Biden
will give a tour

00:21:36.300 --> 00:21:38.200
of the White House
holiday decorations

00:21:38.200 --> 00:21:41.000
for an HGTV Christmas special.

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:42.067
Yeah, and after that, stay tuned

00:21:42.067 --> 00:21:43.734
for Melania's
decoration special,

00:21:43.734 --> 00:21:45.434
"The Nightmare
Before Christmas."

00:21:45.434 --> 00:21:49.934
[ Laughter ]

00:21:49.934 --> 00:21:51.767
Let's get to some news.
I saw a new poll

00:21:51.767 --> 00:21:53.501
that said President Biden's
approval rating

00:21:53.501 --> 00:21:55.701
is now up to 46%.

00:21:55.701 --> 00:21:56.934
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:21:56.934 --> 00:21:59.434
46%, that's pretty much
the blood-alcohol content

00:21:59.434 --> 00:22:01.033
of everyone at SantaCon.

00:22:01.033 --> 00:22:02.567
[ Laughter ]

00:22:02.567 --> 00:22:04.834
I like that we're cool
with 46% for a president,

00:22:04.834 --> 00:22:06.868
but if a restaurant
had 2 1/2 stars on Yelp,

00:22:06.868 --> 00:22:08.033
we'd call
the health department.

00:22:08.033 --> 00:22:09.234
[ Laughter ]

00:22:09.234 --> 00:22:10.767
Did you guys see this?
A top adviser

00:22:10.767 --> 00:22:11.968
to Senator Bernie Sanders

00:22:11.968 --> 00:22:14.367
said that if Biden
doesn't run in 2024,

00:22:14.367 --> 00:22:16.133
Sanders will give it
a hard look.

00:22:16.133 --> 00:22:17.367
[ Laughter ]

00:22:17.367 --> 00:22:18.834
Yeah, people weren't sure
about him

00:22:18.834 --> 00:22:20.634
the last two elections,
but maybe they'll vote for him

00:22:20.634 --> 00:22:22.267
now that he's more mature.

00:22:22.267 --> 00:22:27.267
[ Laughter ]

00:22:27.267 --> 00:22:28.734
Some more big news
from Washington.

00:22:28.734 --> 00:22:30.534
Today, Senator Kyrsten Sinema
announced

00:22:30.534 --> 00:22:32.434
that she's leaving
the Democratic Party

00:22:32.434 --> 00:22:34.968
and registering
as an Independent.

00:22:34.968 --> 00:22:36.868
It's good timing, 'cause
nothing says the holiday season

00:22:36.868 --> 00:22:38.534
like leaving a party early.
Right?

00:22:38.534 --> 00:22:39.701
[ Laughter ]

00:22:39.701 --> 00:22:40.968
Well, listen to this.

00:22:40.968 --> 00:22:42.701
I heard that if Putin loses
the war in Ukraine,

00:22:42.701 --> 00:22:45.601
he's going to flee
to South America.

00:22:45.601 --> 00:22:47.501
Yeah, and he has his disguise
all planned out.

00:22:47.501 --> 00:22:48.901
He's gonna wear a shirt.

00:22:48.901 --> 00:22:55.667
[ Laughter ]

00:22:55.667 --> 00:22:56.868
Thank you.

00:22:56.868 --> 00:22:57.868
[ Laughter ]

00:22:57.868 --> 00:22:58.934
[ Rim shot ]

00:22:58.934 --> 00:23:00.834
Thank you.

00:23:00.834 --> 00:23:03.534
Some business news --
Apple has a new iMessage feature

00:23:03.534 --> 00:23:04.968
that will alert both users

00:23:04.968 --> 00:23:08.934
if they were being spied on
by a state-sponsored attacker.

00:23:08.934 --> 00:23:10.334
Yeah, it's never good seeing

00:23:10.334 --> 00:23:11.734
"North Korea
has entered the chat."

00:23:11.734 --> 00:23:14.067
And you go...
[ Laughter ]

00:23:14.067 --> 00:23:15.334
Some entertainment news.

00:23:15.334 --> 00:23:17.434
I read that the
Miss Universe Pageant is moving

00:23:17.434 --> 00:23:21.000
from broadcast TV to streaming
on the Roku Channel.

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:23.067
Yep, and now the winner
of the talent portion

00:23:23.067 --> 00:23:25.367
is whoever can find
the Roku Channel.

00:23:25.367 --> 00:23:27.200
[ Laughter ]

00:23:27.200 --> 00:23:28.501
When asked how
they felt about it,

00:23:28.501 --> 00:23:31.601
a representative for the pageant
said, "World peace."

00:23:31.601 --> 00:23:32.801
[ Laughter ]

00:23:32.801 --> 00:23:34.534
Guys, last night in L.A.,

00:23:34.534 --> 00:23:35.901
there was a big
video-game award show

00:23:35.901 --> 00:23:37.200
called The Game Awards, okay?

00:23:37.200 --> 00:23:38.467
And they got a pretty huge actor
to present.

00:23:38.467 --> 00:23:39.901
Take a look at this.

00:23:39.901 --> 00:23:44.400
-Please join me in welcoming
to the Game Awards, Al Pacino.

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:46.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:23:46.534 --> 00:23:49.200
-But, uh, I -- I -- I --

00:23:49.200 --> 00:23:52.133
I'm -- It's hard for me
to see the teleprompter.

00:23:52.133 --> 00:23:53.567
[ Laughter ]

00:23:53.567 --> 00:23:57.400
I don't play
a whole lot of video games.

00:23:57.400 --> 00:24:00.868
[ Laughter ]

00:24:00.868 --> 00:24:02.634
[ Rim shot ]

00:24:02.634 --> 00:24:05.033
-Wha-- Wha-- What?

00:24:05.033 --> 00:24:07.100
[ Laughter continues ]

00:24:07.100 --> 00:24:09.767
-It was Pacino's
most challenging role yet,

00:24:09.767 --> 00:24:11.400
"guy who wants to be here."

00:24:11.400 --> 00:24:12.834
[ Laughter ]

00:24:12.834 --> 00:24:14.434
I don't know if he
played "Super Mario Bros.,"

00:24:14.434 --> 00:24:16.033
but he definitely
ate a mushroom.

00:24:16.033 --> 00:24:18.534
[ Laughter ]

00:24:18.534 --> 00:24:20.033
Once the mushrooms
wear off, he's like,

00:24:20.033 --> 00:24:21.968
"Say hello
to my little friend."

00:24:21.968 --> 00:24:23.167
[ Mario shrinking sound ]

00:24:23.167 --> 00:24:26.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:24:26.567 --> 00:24:27.701
Thank you.
I do space work.

00:24:27.701 --> 00:24:30.534
-Yeah, wow, space work,
very good.

00:24:30.534 --> 00:24:31.801
-Hey, this is going viral.

00:24:31.801 --> 00:24:35.133
A man, who was out kayaking,
saw a great white shark.

00:24:35.133 --> 00:24:37.334
Yeah, and then, when he asked
his friend what he should do,

00:24:37.334 --> 00:24:38.767
his friend had
a very interesting response.

00:24:38.767 --> 00:24:40.467
Watch this.

00:24:40.467 --> 00:24:42.234
-Dude, Danny.

00:24:42.234 --> 00:24:44.200
-Yeah.
-What do I do?

00:24:46.567 --> 00:24:48.267
Holy [bleep]
-Film it.

00:24:48.267 --> 00:24:49.400
-Holy [bleep]

00:24:49.400 --> 00:24:56.767
[ Laughter ]

00:24:56.767 --> 00:24:57.934
-Honestly, at that point,

00:24:57.934 --> 00:24:59.334
what else can you really do,
I guess?

00:24:59.334 --> 00:25:02.400
He was like, "Uh, now slap it
with a tortilla!"

00:25:02.400 --> 00:25:03.467
[ Laughter ]

00:25:03.467 --> 00:25:06.901
"Slap the shark
with a tortilla!"

00:25:06.901 --> 00:25:09.601
And finally, a puppy was found
after he escaped from his home

00:25:09.601 --> 00:25:13.968
in Manhattan and swam across
the Hudson River to New Jersey.

00:25:13.968 --> 00:25:15.601
He swam all the way
to New Jersey

00:25:15.601 --> 00:25:17.467
just to get away from SantaCon.

